1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,332
Next time you get a window seat on a plane,

2
00:00:04,352 --> 00:00:07,044
look at the bottom of the window.

3
00:00:07,274 --> 00:00:08,877
There's a tiny hole.

4
00:00:09,107 --> 00:00:10,660
It's not a crack,

5
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,646
and it's not a defect.

6
00:00:12,876 --> 00:00:14,429
It's there on purpose,

7
00:00:14,449 --> 00:00:16,778
and it quietly does two jobs.

8
00:00:17,378 --> 00:00:19,657
Most people assume a plane window

9
00:00:19,677 --> 00:00:21,280
is one thick sheet.

10
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:22,749
It's actually three.

11
00:00:23,349 --> 00:00:25,265
The pane you can touch

12
00:00:25,285 --> 00:00:27,251
is just a scratch shield.

13
00:00:27,481 --> 00:00:30,173
It holds back no pressure at all.

14
00:00:30,403 --> 00:00:33,046
Behind it sit two strong acrylic panes:

15
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:35,758
a middle one and an outer one.

16
00:00:36,358 --> 00:00:37,548
At cruising altitude,

17
00:00:37,568 --> 00:00:39,534
the air outside is thin.

18
00:00:39,764 --> 00:00:42,406
The air inside is kept much denser,

19
00:00:42,426 --> 00:00:45,068
so it pushes outward on every window

20
00:00:45,088 --> 00:00:47,417
with hundreds of kilos of force.

21
00:00:48,017 --> 00:00:49,207
That tiny hole

22
00:00:49,227 --> 00:00:51,193
goes through the middle pane.

23
00:00:51,423 --> 00:00:54,429
Cabin air flows into the gap behind it,

24
00:00:54,449 --> 00:00:56,364
so the middle pane feels

25
00:00:56,384 --> 00:00:58,350
equal pressure on both sides.

26
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,223
The outer pane carries the whole load,

27
00:01:01,243 --> 00:01:03,159
and the middle pane waits,

28
00:01:03,179 --> 00:01:04,781
unstressed, as a backup.

29
00:01:05,381 --> 00:01:06,571
Job number two:

30
00:01:06,591 --> 00:01:08,870
that same airflow lets moisture escape,

31
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:12,309
so the gap stays clear of fog and frost.

32
00:01:12,909 --> 00:01:14,149
One tiny hole.

33
00:01:14,379 --> 00:01:16,708
A spare window and a defogger.

34
00:01:16,938 --> 00:01:18,127
What everyday thing

35
00:01:18,147 --> 00:01:19,750
should we unpack next?
